infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title The honest progression: when to add a specialized store
  desc Don't reach for the buzzword — escalate only when a measured limit forces it
  order asc
  sequences
    - label Start on the primary
      desc One store. Postgres does full-text (tsvector) and time-series (TimescaleDB) well enough at modest scale — far cheaper than the consistency cost of two.
    - label Specialize on a measured limit
      desc The metrics firehose crowds out OLTP, or LIKE scans millions of rows and times out. The measured limit — not the buzzword — justifies the second store.
    - label Treat it as a derived index
      desc The primary stays the source of truth; the search / time-series store is a read-optimized projection. Lose it and you rebuild from the primary — only that query path, never data.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #10b981
